  "retained_change": "The general Sturm search no longer stops after 256 successful dyadic steps. It carries domain/represented-root boundary ownership through subdivision, constructs intervals only for retained singleton candidates, and discards certified-empty children immediately. Root-count differences and midpoint variation ordering are checked instead of saturating an inconsistent count to zero.",
  "exactness": {
    "reproduced_failure": "On 96a34ee, the public unit isolator returned Uncertain(Ordering) for the exact rational root 2^-300. The new regression was run and failed before the implementation change.",
    "certificate": "Every continuing midpoint is a certified non-root whose variations partition its parent's count. Unavailable point or ordering evidence still returns explicit uncertainty. Represented midpoint roots still return for deflation; singletons retain the shared authoritative Sturm sequence.",
    "boundary_ownership": "Every initial partition boundary is a domain endpoint or a previously represented root. Only these original sides retain their ownership flag after splitting; a certified non-root midpoint is never an original boundary. This replaces repeated scans and exact endpoint comparisons without weakening ownership.",
    "regression_queries": {
      "public_unit_interval": 72,
      "finite_extension_intervals": 36,
      "inverted_variation_rejections": 2,
      "coverage": "Both policies; 300- and 600-bit boundary separations; rational dyadic and nondyadic roots; repeated roots; an irrational root; a root close to an already represented root; positive/negative rational and pi scaling; both ends of negative and exterior finite domains.",
      "names": [
        "unit_root_isolation_has_no_fixed_dyadic_depth_limit",
        "finite_interval_isolation_has_no_fixed_dyadic_depth_limit",
        "carried_sturm_variations_match_partition_root_counts"
      ]
    },
    "trace_accounting": "Discarded empty children are now counted when their variation equality proves emptiness. The boundary benchmark keeps the same 130 bisections and maximum depth 130, but counts 263 intervals instead of 134: the old search discarded many queued empty children without visiting them when its represented-root return restarted isolation. No additional Sturm midpoint evaluations are introduced by this accounting.",
    "public_api_added": false,
    "compatibility_shims_added": false
  },
